WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.680
Really? You landed your dream job at the company, Obata?

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.280
It's all thanks to what I learned at your seminars, Professor.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.740
Oy, oy! Give the "Professor" thing a rest!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.950
Right now, I'm just a middle-aged florist.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.320
Your dad used to lecture at a university? {Added 'an.' We Americans don't use 'university' as a standalone noun.}{Changed to 'a'. Insert deaf joke here.}

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.570
They still occasionally ask him to come give lectures.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.960
Really?!

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.500
I didn't know he was that distinguished...

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.000
So what do you do at your company?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.010
I work in the planning and sales
 department, promoting our flowers.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.970
Though more often than not, I'm just given everyone's odd jobs!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.590
Well, that's great!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.140
So what brings you here today?

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.270
I've actually come to ask you for a favor.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.230
Professor, I implore you to come join our company!

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.140
Huh?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.890
Huh?

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:49.000
{OP}

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.190
HeartCatch

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.650
Precure!

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.240
HeartCatch Precure!

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.200
Now, all together

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.710
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.670
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.290
Within each of our chests,

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.960
they begin to sprout

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.640
The seeds of the heart

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.930
are growing

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.550
bit by bit

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.220
Red,

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:22.840
white

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.130
and yellow

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.890
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.310
all varied colors

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.770
that they

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.980
shine so brightly!

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.320
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.820
with such care

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.530
will never wither

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.080
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.960
Now, all together

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.450
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.120
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:59.000
They're always right by our sides

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.840
So together

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.720
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.640
bloom even more!

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.140
HeartCatch

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.650
Precure!

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.950
My Father's Been Scouted<i>!</i>

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.950
My Father's Been Scouted<i>!</i>

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.750
You dad is a really impressive scholar, isn't he?

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.330
And your mom's glasses make her look brainy too, don't they?

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.680
What did she do?

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.850
My mother did clerical work at a company called Red Florian. {"My mother worked did." I stare disapprovingly at you and remove the 'worked.'}

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.010
Red Florian?!

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.220
That really chic florist all the celebs and stars use?!

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.720
Which means their meeting had some connection to flowers?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.890
That's right!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.550
Dad was doing research at the botanical gardens...

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.000
And Mom was searching for a flower that Red Florian was looking for...

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.540
I'm so sorry! Are you all right?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.970
Yeah. Sorry about...

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.470
The two of them met amongst the fields of spring.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.270
What an amazing man...

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.400
You are more beautiful than any flower...

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.320
Let's get married!

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.210
Yes!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.770
That pacing's way too fast!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.040
No, I think that's pretty much how it went.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.010
They fell in love at first sight and got married within a month, apparently.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:43.530
Seriously?!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.080
A fateful encounter amongst the flowers...

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.830
It's kinda cliché...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:49.790
but awesome!

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.420
Isn't it?!

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.670
Even I'm kinda envious...

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.950
Your family gets all the luck, huh?

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.410
Your dad's gonna get a really great job...

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.870
Looks like you Hanasakis have a lot to celebrate!

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.670
Hooray! Hooray!

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.470
Something wrong?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.950
It's nothing.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.230
Tada! I've made your favorite, Tsubomi! Meat and potato stew!

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.570
What's the matter, Tsubomi?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.240
Dad... are you going to join Obata's company?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.290
I refused his offer.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.950
Huh? Why?!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.670
Being florists keeps our hearts burning far more than our research ever did.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:37.650
Right?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.750
Yup!

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:45.220
I enjoy being able to sit down and eat with you guys far too much to give it up that easily!

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.520
Now then, we should eat this lovely meal before it gets cold, shouldn't we?

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.190
Yeah! Let's dig in! {tlnote: 'let's dig in' means itadakimasu!}

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.420
Okay, okay, try to answer this one.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:09.620
A dog that likes pork cutlet and a cat that likes deep fried seafood played chess against each other.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.870
Which one won...

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.460
No, I think I've got everything there covered.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:16.950
Right.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.000
Right.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.130
Excuse me, then.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.380
Huh? Isn't that the guy from before?

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.940
I've been waiting, Tsubomi.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:30.600
The offer I made your father was a very good one.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.990
But no matter how many times I ask him, he always says no.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.890
Huh?! Your dad declined the offer?!

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.010
Why?! What gives?!

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.360
Your father is both talented and extremely knowledgeable.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.080
Won't you please help me convince him?!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.080
Tsubomi, please! I'm begging you!

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.000
Stoooooooop!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.160
I have a suggestion!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.380
Rather than standing around here talking, why don't we go somewhere else and discuss this?

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.800
Well? Let's go.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.180
The weight and temperature of the sand induces perspiration.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.440
Bathing in sand truly does wonders for the skin.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:28.400
Now my skin shall become smoother, 
and I shall be all the more beautiful for it.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:32.110
Hey, Snacky. More sand on my soles, please.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.170
A message from Professor Sabark? What is it?

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.190
Hurry and defeat the Precure?

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:49.600
I'm taking a nice hot desert bath at the 
moment for my complexion. I'll do it later. {Deserty -> desert because it sounds dumb and not at all French. Also removed the comma after complexion.}

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:02.440
The Precure are no match for the likes of the most beautiful Lord Kobraja? {Questionmark inside quotes. Also, do we really need to keep the 'sama?'}

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.380
I am <i>most</i> beautiful...

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:13.810
The Precure are waiting to behold Lord Kobraja's beauty? {Questionmark inside quotes.}

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.660
I suppose if I must...

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.470
Then I shall allow them to feast themselves upon my beauty!

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.670
Be grateful, Precures!

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.230
This is...

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.390
Isn't this a Drosera obovata?!

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:52.720
Whoa! There's even Hypericum kinashianums! {Yes, I went and googled to confirm that the second part of that horrible name should be lowercase. Even though it looks dumb. Ugh.}

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.920
Do you know this one? It's an Acystopteris japonica.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.360
Of course I do!

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:59.790
The spores that grow on the underside of an Acystopteris really are beautiful...

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.640
They're so pretty...

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.950
Ferns really are interesting, aren't they?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:04.540
They sure are!

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:08.250
They're nerding out so hard I can't follow at all... {on -> talking}

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.210
You're very well informed, Obata.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.610
That's because I love them!

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.600
So, Tsubomi, to continue our discussion from before...

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.550
Excuse me a moment.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:21.930
Hello, this is Obata.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.260
Yes, everything's fine.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.260
Not at all.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.270
He's really not helping things.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.780
I guess he's just really busy at work.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.590
Yes, if you'd please.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.140
Excuse me, then.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.320
Sorry about that!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.490
Sounds like you're bogged down with work.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:39.590
Yeah, a bit.

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:42.540
But if I don't work hard, we'll lose out to the other companies.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.500
That's why I really need your father's help. {Rewrote this line a little bit. It was originally "And so we don't, I really need your father's help..." which made very little sense.}

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.170
So please, Tsubomi, won't you help me out?

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.170
I'm begging you!

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.350
Do you hate Obata, Tsubomi?

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.310
O-Of course I don't!

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:04.990
Right. After all, you were really 
enjoying your conversation earlier.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:08.120
So you must have some reason for being so hesitant, right?

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.030
If you don't tell us, neither Obata nor I will understand, you know?

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:26.290
I don't think there's a "winning" or "losing" approach to flowers.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.250
Huh?

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.780
All of these flowers have their own unique merits.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.960
So even if you don't have some new species, it doesn't really matter.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:38.180
That might be fine for you, but I have a job to do!

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.790
If I don't create flowers that'll sell, I won't win!

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.430
You're just a child, so you might not understand, but...

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.870
Children have hearts too, you know?

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:48.020
Grandma!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.640
Professor Hanasaki!

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:50.730
It's been a while.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.180
Grandma, you know Obata?

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.560
Indeed.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.980
Back when he was a student, he used to come here every now and again.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.740
He's matured into quite the young man.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.620
Oh, you're too kind.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.830
You remind me of how Youichi and Mizuki were back in the day.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:07.830
Huh?

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:13.200
The two of them were always so busy with their work.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.340
They were traveling around Japan, and sometimes around the world.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.930
They were constantly leaving on some business or another...

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:28.700
And while they were away, I always
 watched over Tsubomi in their stead.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.800
Tsubomi always saw them off with a smile on her face.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.670
But one day, they finally realized...

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.740
that while they were working so hard to support their family...

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.370
that very family had come apart at the seams.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.570
After that, the two of them quit their jobs and opened the flower shop here in Kibougahana.{Kibougahana isn't mentioned by name, but I thought it'd be a good idea to mention the city name again. It's BEEN A WHILE.}

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.680
Tsubomi was more important to them than their jobs, so they chose to live as a family once more.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.280
So that's what happened...

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:13.830
If he accepted your job offer, then he might've had to watch his family come apart like that again.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.860
Was that not why Youichi declined it in the first place?

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.710
That's...

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.610
I think creating new flowers is something truly amazing.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.430
But...

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.470
I'm sorry.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:34.200
Yes.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.010
Yes!

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.980
I'm very sorry!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.030
Yes, as soon as I can.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.440
If you would.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.390
That's a rather sullen face you're wearing.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:53.330
I'll be taking that discolored Flower of your Heart!

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.880
Flower of the Heart, your moment has come!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:11.560
Desertrian, that's your cue!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:19.580
Tsubomi, I'm sorry about before. I said some pretty selfish things without realizing the situation.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:25.490
It's all right. Because you were there, I was able to tell Obata how I really felt.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.490
I see!

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.750
What was that sound just now?!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.680
A Desertrian!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:48.720
Tsubomi, look at that!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.390
Obata!

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.470
We have to save him!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.220
Right!

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.880
Go, Seeds of the Precure!

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.320
Precure!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.440
Open My Heart!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.550
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.770
Cure Blossom!

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:10.280
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.880
Cure Marine!

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:22.290
HeartCatch Precure!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.120
Now then, my dear Precure!

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.360
I have come, just as you wished!

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.120
Allow your eyes to feast upon my radiance to your heart's content!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.230
Huh?

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.730
What on earth are you going on about?

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.620
Nobody's been waiting for you!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.170
What did you say?! {I love his expression here.}

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:44.540
And I even halted my makeover for you...

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.450
Go get them, Desertrian!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.530
Cellphoooone!

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:57.680
Blossom!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.310
Ceeeellphone!

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.080
Marine!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.680
Are you all right?!

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:28.710
What's with that thing?! It's unpredictable and so fast... {It's because they actually paid the animation team to do QUALITY ACTION this time round. Noticeably different.}

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.680
I also wish to do research!

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:37.640
Huh?!

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:41.600
I also yearn to create new flowers!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.730
That's my dream! {Needs the apostrophe here.}

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:47.690
Obata's... dream?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.800
But I can't tell them that.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:56.350
If I told them I wanted to join the
 research team, they might fire me!

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:58.030
I don't want that!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.990
These are Obata's true feelings?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:12.920
Watch out!

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:28.220
I want to do research...

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:30.230
but I'm too scared to say it!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.510
Hmph! What a coward!

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:45.160
Someone like you is capable of nothing!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.370
That's not true!

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:52.840
What made Obata so anxious was the fact that he loved working with flowers!

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.550
It's because his feelings were serious that he became so scared!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.870
All of this is irrelevant. {This would be a good spot to go FRENCHITY FRENCH if you haven't anywhere else in the ep.}

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:01.760
If a Flower of the Heart is usable, I shall use it.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:08.520
I won't forgive you for playing with Obata's hardworking heart!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.440
I've had it up to here with this!

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:18.200
My heart may be vaster than the sea, but this is as much as it can take!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.890
No matter how fast he is, there's only one of him!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:24.950
And two of us! {Her mouth starts moving well before this line starts. Can you push it back a little?}

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.140
Precure Double Shoot!

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.060
Non! There's dust on my beautiful face!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.690
Now's your chance!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.990
Gather, Floral Power!

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.700
Blossom Tact!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:10.120
Marine Tact!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:19.020
Gather, Dual Floral Power!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:24.680
Precure Floral Power Fortissimo!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.780
Heart Catch!

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.120
Now I'll have to restart my makeover!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:09.990
So what'd Obata say?

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:12.700
That he'd given up trying to recruit Dad.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:17.090
And someday, he'd like to be able to do his own research, but lacks the confidence right now.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:18.870
Eavesdropping again?

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.750
I-I'm sorry!

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.230
Excuse me!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:25.280
Um, I'd like a sunflower, please!

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:30.640
I'm sorry, but sunflowers aren't in bloom right now.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.250
Whaaat?!

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:36.700
Sunflowers love the summer,
 when the sun is at its happiest!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:41.470
In order to make a flower truly
 beautiful, it needs time to grow!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.650
So when summer comes, please come back, okay?

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:50.330
I'll keep the biggest and prettiest sunflower for you!

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.280
Really?!

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:52.390
Really! I promise!

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.330
Then pinky swear on it, 'kay?

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.190
Okay!

00:20:55.190 --> 00:21:01.070
Cross my heart, hope to die, stick a needle in my eye.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.310
You're a bit like a sunflower in the spring yourself. {This needs to get moved above the other line if it's really a voiceover.}

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:02.070
It's a promise!

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.070
Huh?

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:08.030
In order to make the flower of your dream bloom, isn't this where you need to work hard and grow stronger? {You -> your}

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.330
Yes. That's what I'm going to do.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:13.500
I don't know how many years it'll take, but I'll challenge myself!

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.330
That's the Obata I know!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.440
Give that here!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:27.180
The Flower of his Heart has been revived!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.440
In the language of flowers, a white hyacinth means "serene love." {Period inside quotes.}

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:35.890
By returning his flower-loving heart, we've made him happy again!

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.070
I think a Heart Seed's about to be born...

